I have a soul but this;
I am a creature of the sea,
And I am a sea of life.

Each that is lost is part of me;

Each is lost in me is part thereof;
And each that is gained is part me.

My river is not a river,
Nor a river a river;
Nor an ocean a sea;
And yet, as a bird,
I am a bird of the sea.

That I had heard before;
I found it to every prayer
That had been given.

I could not believe it,
But I knew it was true;
It was the only
